  "details": "<p>The territory of the <em>tribus Voltinia\u00a0</em>may be indicated by an imperial inscription, which lists the number of men who received free grain. Its location might be found on the left bank of the river Tiber, above the <em>tribus Voturia</em>.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The tribus Voltinia (or Votinia) was an older rural tribe of ancient Rome.",
